          text: 'The O–H bond is strongly polarized, and alcohols both donate and accept [[gchem-hydrogen-bond|hydrogen bonds]]. Boiling an alcohol means breaking a network of O–H···O contacts, so alcohols boil far higher than ethers or alkanes of similar mass.',
