          text: 'Water solubility follows the same logic. Methanol, ethanol and propanol mix with water in all proportions; butan-1-ol dissolves only to about 8 g per 100 mL, and hexan-1-ol to under 1 g. As a rule of thumb, one OH group can carry about three or four carbons into water. Glucose, with five OH groups on six carbons, is very soluble.',
