          text: 'The conjugate base, an [[ochem-alkoxide|alkoxide]] ($\\ce{RO-}$), is a strong base and a good nucleophile. To make it completely, use a base whose conjugate acid is much weaker than the alcohol: sodium hydride ($\\ce{NaH}$, conjugate acid $\\ce{H2}$ with $\\mathrm{p}K_a \\approx 35$) or sodium metal ($\\ce{2ROH + 2Na -> 2RONa + H2}$). Hydroxide is not strong enough, as the [[gchem-pka|pKa]] values show:',
